            </ul>
        </How>

        <Summary>
            <ul>
                <li>Use one bounded xUnit fixture to start, probe, and dispose the real AppHost graph.</li>
                <li>Inject that fixture into PageTest while keeping a fresh browser context per test.</li>
                <li>Drive an existing business workflow through the UI and verify its persisted result after navigation.</li>
                <li>Keep test records unique; a fresh host seed does not reset data between methods.</li>
                <li>Use disposable resources and normal fixture teardown instead of writing to shared staging data.</li>
                <li>For cross-team events, pin container images and assert consumer side effects—not just broker health—in the UI.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                <strong>What to read next:</strong> for the topology this fixture starts, revisit
                <a class="underline" href="/blogs/getting-started-with-aspire-in-dotnet/">getting started with Aspire in .NET</a>
                before adapting its resource names and dependencies to your application.
            </p>
        </Summary>
